| `check_V` writer declarations | Refuses a module that writes to the filesystem without `effect: writes` and a `rerun:`, or a `fixed-point` claim without a proof that resolves, and a shell script whose opening comment block states no `effect:`. Python and shell proof sections use `[0-9]{1,4}`; a malformed section stays one FAILURE finding. | `make check` | [`shell.excluded_paths`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.script_suffixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.shebang_shells`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Silent over `tests/` and over shell tests. A write it cannot see is a WARN when declared and invisible when not; a shell write is never seen, so a shell script's `effect:` is judged present, not true. | [idempotency.md](../guides/idempotency.md) | always |
